I released v0.2.0 for #992 and commented on the issue. It was already closed when I went to close it, so nothing else was needed there. Before commenting I checked that the release really went out: the v0.2.0 tag is on origin, the Release workflow run for it passed, and crates.io now lists 0.2.0 as the latest version.

The comment covers:
• **Version:** 0.2.0 rather than 0.1.20, because two new flags were added (--save-session and --continue-strict).
• **CHANGELOG:** the stale [Unreleased] section was rewritten from the 233 commits since v0.1.19.
• **Gate:** build, test, clippy and fmt all passed on the release commit.
• **Pricing table:** still not checked against vendor prices. The audit found 9 drifted models and 137 of 173 unpriced, and the CHANGELOG says so.
• **yoagent:** bumped to 0.24.1. The `retry_safe_events` change from #991 is not in this release; it was reverted because it drops the final failure's text when output goes to a pipe.
• **Ctrl+C check:** an interrupted -p run stops cleanly. It still exits 0, though, and the interrupt notice goes to stdout. Both are tracked in #993.

